WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.072 --> 00:00:02.198
- He's a basketball player who currently

00:00:02.198 --> 00:00:03.941
plays for the LA Lakers.

00:00:03.941 --> 00:00:06.629
- He's a 17 time NBA All Star.

00:00:06.629 --> 00:00:09.408
- He became the youngest
player in NBA history

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:11.760
to reach 30,000 career points.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:12.909
- He's Kobe Bryant,

00:00:12.909 --> 00:00:16.156
and here are his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:16.156 --> 00:00:18.744
(dramatic swoop)

00:00:18.744 --> 00:00:19.650
(basketball bouncing)

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:20.698
- There's a choice

00:00:20.698 --> 00:00:22.916
we have to make as people, as individuals.

00:00:22.916 --> 00:00:25.286
If you want to be great at something,

00:00:25.286 --> 00:00:26.697
you have to make inherent sacrifices

00:00:26.697 --> 00:00:27.998
that come along with that.

00:00:27.998 --> 00:00:31.412
Family time, hanging
out with your friends.

00:00:31.412 --> 00:00:33.545
It was at the age of 18, I knew that I

00:00:33.545 --> 00:00:37.953
was not going to be
stopped. This was my life.

00:00:37.953 --> 00:00:40.764
We all can be masters at our craft,

00:00:40.764 --> 00:00:41.843
but you have to make sacrifices

00:00:41.843 --> 00:00:43.924
that come along with making that decision.

00:00:43.924 --> 00:00:45.028
(hip hop beat)

00:00:45.028 --> 00:00:46.593
(crowd cheers)

00:00:46.593 --> 00:00:48.497
- [Commentator] Look at
the hustle of Lamar Odom.

00:00:48.497 --> 00:00:49.888
- [Commentator] Off to Kobe Bryant!

00:00:49.888 --> 00:00:51.726
(crowd cheers)

00:00:51.726 --> 00:00:54.468
- [Commentator] And Kobe, with emphasis.

00:00:54.468 --> 00:00:55.858
- Once you have the passion, a thing

00:00:55.858 --> 00:00:57.263
that you're passionate about now,

00:00:57.263 --> 00:01:00.399
you can look at other
people, or other entities,

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:02.714
or other things, or works of art.

00:01:02.714 --> 00:01:06.184
You can draw things from
that to help you be better

00:01:06.184 --> 00:01:09.989
at what you do, by looking
for those common denominators.

00:01:09.989 --> 00:01:13.240
Johnny wanted to know how do I prepare.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.155
How do I prepare? How do I
study? How do I view the game?

00:01:16.155 --> 00:01:18.405
How do you build your game?

00:01:19.506 --> 00:01:23.009
My response is much like
the way he builds products.

00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:24.906
You think sequentially.

00:01:24.906 --> 00:01:28.159
You look at the end result
that you want to create,

00:01:28.159 --> 00:01:30.699
but in order to create that,
there's so many little things

00:01:30.699 --> 00:01:34.354
that go into this
massive entity or device.

00:01:34.354 --> 00:01:37.166
It's no different than
building my basketball game.

00:01:37.166 --> 00:01:40.292
You start with what you
want your game to be?

00:01:40.292 --> 00:01:44.033
What would make your game most unstoppable

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:47.586
or hard to deal with? Now
you work backwards from there

00:01:47.586 --> 00:01:50.469
and you start building
it one piece at a time,

00:01:50.469 --> 00:01:53.712
one move at a time, one counter at a time.

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:55.587
There's a lot of similarities there.

00:01:55.587 --> 00:01:57.351
(hip hop beat)

00:01:57.351 --> 00:01:59.274
- [Commentator] Artest
looking, gets it to Bryant.

00:01:59.274 --> 00:02:02.323
Bryant dribbling, has to
put it up at the buzzer.

00:02:02.323 --> 00:02:03.314
(game buzzer)
Backs it in!

00:02:03.314 --> 00:02:07.077
(laughs) He backs in the three!

00:02:07.077 --> 00:02:08.966
And the Lakers win the game!

00:02:08.966 --> 00:02:10.853
(crowd cheers)

00:02:10.853 --> 00:02:14.324
- [Commentator] And that is
just greatness, personified.

00:02:14.324 --> 00:02:17.657
- You just got to have the fearlessness to

00:02:17.657 --> 00:02:20.917
really take those shots.
Because you miss those shots,

00:02:20.917 --> 00:02:23.451
then you have to deal with the criticism,

00:02:23.451 --> 00:02:24.887
you have to deal with...

00:02:24.887 --> 00:02:26.079
- Us taking about it, right?

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:27.561
- [Kobe] Right!

00:02:27.561 --> 00:02:29.510
And a lot of times, a lot of
people kind of get a little

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:31.769
apprehensive about taking
those shots because of that.

00:02:31.769 --> 00:02:33.173
- While we mentioned it, it
seemed like you started smiling

00:02:33.173 --> 00:02:37.385
already just thinking
about the word criticism!

00:02:37.385 --> 00:02:41.448
- It's always been a myth to
me as to why certain people

00:02:41.448 --> 00:02:45.629
don't really like those situations
because of the pressure.

00:02:45.629 --> 00:02:48.072
Because we've all lost games before.

00:02:48.072 --> 00:02:49.642
So it's not like by you missing that shot,

00:02:49.642 --> 00:02:51.122
you're about to face something
that you will never face

00:02:51.122 --> 00:02:53.273
again or haven't faced in the past.

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:57.217
We've all come up short
at one time or another.

00:02:57.217 --> 00:02:59.394
You just got to kind
of let it all hang out,

00:02:59.394 --> 00:03:02.235
and trust your skills and
trust the work that you put in.

00:03:02.235 --> 00:03:03.425
(hip hop beat)

00:03:03.425 --> 00:03:05.743
- [Commentator] Now Bryant
again, out between the rings,

00:03:05.743 --> 00:03:08.021
guarded by Pippen. Kobe on the move.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.066
Lobs for O'Neal (mumbles)

00:03:10.066 --> 00:03:12.352
Kobe Bryant worked into the lane,

00:03:12.352 --> 00:03:14.994
and Shaq hammered him
in with the right hand.

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:16.954
Time out Portland.

00:03:16.954 --> 00:03:18.288
- So that means taking things,

00:03:18.288 --> 00:03:21.754
using things in your life that are scars.

00:03:21.754 --> 00:03:25.004
Using those moments as a weapon, right?

00:03:27.118 --> 00:03:29.534
Using basketball as kind of like a vehicle

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:32.271
through which to express yourself.

00:03:32.271 --> 00:03:35.152
So at that moment, for us
to face the Celtics again,

00:03:35.152 --> 00:03:38.302
it's not about the Celtics.
It's not about your opponent.

00:03:38.302 --> 00:03:41.711
It's about you. It's about you
taking your inner struggles,

00:03:41.711 --> 00:03:44.711
and channeling that through the game

00:03:46.271 --> 00:03:47.938
as a way to unleash.

00:03:48.778 --> 00:03:51.245
So now it became a matter of
how do I express that to them,

00:03:51.245 --> 00:03:52.695
how do I get them to that point

00:03:52.695 --> 00:03:55.226
where they figure this out for themselves.

00:03:55.226 --> 00:03:57.350
Because I can't say "Hey listen,
I need you to play harder."

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:58.558
- [Host] So what'd you do?

00:03:58.558 --> 00:03:59.960
- Well, I had to share my story.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:03.072
I had to open up to
them, and let them know,

00:04:03.072 --> 00:04:05.693
I've dealt with things. This
is the things that I use.

00:04:05.693 --> 00:04:07.683
This is how I go about focus.

00:04:07.683 --> 00:04:09.562
This is how I deal with adversity.

00:04:09.562 --> 00:04:12.297
This is how I deal with
arguing with my wife

00:04:12.297 --> 00:04:14.421
the day of the game, and
showing up to the game

00:04:14.421 --> 00:04:16.831
and still having that
focus to be able to play.

00:04:16.831 --> 00:04:19.960
I use those things to open up with them,

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:23.127
and then in turn, they were able to...

00:04:24.525 --> 00:04:28.536
to take those stories
and make them their own.

00:04:28.536 --> 00:04:29.966
(hip hop beat)

00:04:29.966 --> 00:04:31.306
- [Commentator] The Lakers
because of this man,

00:04:31.306 --> 00:04:35.176
Kobe Bryant, can take
over (mumbles). Oh, wow.

00:04:35.176 --> 00:04:37.402
- [Commentator] He
posterizes Dwight Howard.

00:04:37.402 --> 00:04:39.240
(laughter)

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.377
He almost threw his elbow
under the basket that time.

00:04:42.377 --> 00:04:44.422
- Well, you just got to put
one foot in front of the other,

00:04:44.422 --> 00:04:47.920
and sometimes I think, even for myself,

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.032
it's easy to become distracted
a little bit, and start

00:04:50.032 --> 00:04:53.960
trying to look at what the final
pictures going to look like.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.204
When you do that, you can
easily become frustrated

00:04:56.204 --> 00:04:58.995
with where you are at the moment.

00:04:58.995 --> 00:05:02.962
My advice is just to focus on each day and

00:05:02.962 --> 00:05:05.031
have a plan in place of
how you want to improve

00:05:05.031 --> 00:05:07.879
and how you want to get better,
and you stick to that plan

00:05:07.879 --> 00:05:10.197
and trust the fact that every day

00:05:10.197 --> 00:05:14.383
that you stick to the plan will
get you to your end result.

00:05:14.383 --> 00:05:15.991
(hip hop beat)

00:05:15.991 --> 00:05:17.994
- [Commentator] (mumbles)
cannot buy a triple.

00:05:17.994 --> 00:05:21.894
Kobe wheeling, what a play to Turiaf!

00:05:21.894 --> 00:05:22.977
And the foul!

00:05:25.227 --> 00:05:27.507
- [Commentator] And a chance to tie.

00:05:27.507 --> 00:05:31.017
- [Commentator] What a
delivery by Kobe Bryant!

00:05:31.017 --> 00:05:33.350
- I'm not going to be afraid

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:38.926
of confrontation to get
us to where we need to go.

00:05:38.926 --> 00:05:43.228
I think there's a big
misconception when people think

00:05:43.228 --> 00:05:45.244
winning or success comes
from everybody putting their

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:47.239
arms around each other and singing Kumbaya

00:05:47.239 --> 00:05:49.261
and patting them on the
back when they mess up,

00:05:49.261 --> 00:05:51.769
and that's just not reality.
If you're going to be a leader,

00:05:51.769 --> 00:05:53.932
you're not going to please everybody.

00:05:53.932 --> 00:05:55.743
You got to hold people accountable,

00:05:55.743 --> 00:05:58.826
even if you have that moment
of being uncomfortable.

00:05:58.826 --> 00:06:00.058
- You would call a foul on..
- Matter fact,

00:06:00.058 --> 00:06:00.899
get your hands off me.

00:06:00.899 --> 00:06:01.996
Don't touch me the rest of the scrimmage.

00:06:01.996 --> 00:06:02.829
- Alright, we'll see.

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:05.223
- Get your hands off me.

00:06:05.223 --> 00:06:08.083
I always compare it to
sitting across from somebody

00:06:08.083 --> 00:06:10.604
at a dinner table, if we're
sitting across from each other.

00:06:10.604 --> 00:06:13.938
Would you rather sit with a
person that's going to be afraid

00:06:13.938 --> 00:06:16.840
to tell you have something
in between your teeth,

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:19.652
and let you walk around the
restaurant smiling like that

00:06:19.652 --> 00:06:21.608
when you got stuff in between your teeth,

00:06:21.608 --> 00:06:23.137
or would you rather sit with somebody

00:06:23.137 --> 00:06:27.034
that's not afraid to have that
moment of being uncomfortable

00:06:27.034 --> 00:06:30.151
to tell you "You have something
in your teeth," (laughs)

00:06:30.151 --> 00:06:32.119
so you can get it out and
don't look like an idiot

00:06:32.119 --> 00:06:34.404
in front of everybody else, right?

00:06:34.404 --> 00:06:36.525
I'ma tell you if you have
something in your teeth!

00:06:36.525 --> 00:06:38.441
- No matter what, even
if it hurts my feelings?

00:06:38.441 --> 00:06:39.869
- I'ma tell you you have
something in your teeth.

00:06:39.869 --> 00:06:42.016
I'ma tell you and then it's your choice

00:06:42.016 --> 00:06:43.365
if you want to get it out

00:06:43.365 --> 00:06:46.062
or you just want to leave it
there and look like an idiot.

00:06:46.062 --> 00:06:48.253
(hip hop beat)

00:06:48.253 --> 00:06:49.489
- [Commentator] Nice rotation to Bryant.

00:06:49.489 --> 00:06:51.672
Buckle up for Kobe Bryant!

00:06:51.672 --> 00:06:54.952
Kobe Bryant just sucked the gravity

00:06:54.952 --> 00:06:57.186
out of the Target Center, what a play!

00:06:57.186 --> 00:06:58.894
- [Commentator] The Windmill Slam!

00:06:58.894 --> 00:07:00.035
- It's everybody who wants to compete,

00:07:00.035 --> 00:07:03.368
and I think it's knowing how to compete.

00:07:05.334 --> 00:07:09.760
True competitive instinct really
kicks in when you're down.

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:11.518
A lot of people are
competitive at things that

00:07:11.518 --> 00:07:13.935
are rolling their way, and...

00:07:15.184 --> 00:07:18.070
things that they're actually good at.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.979
But it takes a true competitive person

00:07:20.979 --> 00:07:22.197
when things are down like this

00:07:22.197 --> 00:07:24.781
to really step up to the
plate and grab for it.

00:07:24.781 --> 00:07:27.181
(hip hop beat)

00:07:27.181 --> 00:07:28.745
(crowd cheers)

00:07:28.745 --> 00:07:30.759
- [Commentator] Long run
out by Kobe Bryant, behind..

00:07:30.759 --> 00:07:32.957
(cheers)

00:07:32.957 --> 00:07:35.224
What did I just see!?

00:07:35.224 --> 00:07:37.350
- [Commentator] You saw what
Kobe does best, and that's

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:41.867
bring people to their feet
with a sensational play!

00:07:41.867 --> 00:07:45.289
- It's of upmost importance,
like I was such a diehard fan,

00:07:45.289 --> 00:07:48.921
Laker fan growing up, man.
And just my personality,

00:07:48.921 --> 00:07:52.543
for me to ask for a trade or
to go play some place else,

00:07:52.543 --> 00:07:55.637
to try to chase a championship,
that's not me, man.

00:07:55.637 --> 00:07:58.370
That's not what my career has been about,

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:01.858
that's not who I am. I stay with it.

00:08:01.858 --> 00:08:03.374
If the stuff that I've
been through in my life

00:08:03.374 --> 00:08:05.801
and been through in my career
has taught me anything,

00:08:05.801 --> 00:08:07.737
it's the fact that
you'll have good moments,

00:08:07.737 --> 00:08:09.166
you'll have bad moments,
you'll have great moments,

00:08:09.166 --> 00:08:10.596
you'll have horrible
moments, you just keep going

00:08:10.596 --> 00:08:13.753
through all of it, and
things work themselves out.

00:08:13.753 --> 00:08:15.652
(hip hop beat)

00:08:15.652 --> 00:08:16.485
- [Commentator] You've got a dribble,

00:08:16.485 --> 00:08:18.090
got a change of direction by Bryant.

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:20.532
Slam Dunk! (cheers)

00:08:20.532 --> 00:08:23.333
- [Commentator] You talk about
elevation, he went up to the

00:08:23.333 --> 00:08:28.140
rafters before he decided
to put somebody on a poster!

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:31.325
- I've always had some of my
best performances on the road.

00:08:31.325 --> 00:08:33.905
- [Crowd Chants] Kobe sucks! Kobe sucks!

00:08:33.905 --> 00:08:35.978
- [Kobe] When the fans boo,

00:08:35.978 --> 00:08:39.477
I actually love it. I thrive on it.

00:08:39.477 --> 00:08:42.318
They don't understand who I am.

00:08:42.318 --> 00:08:44.793
(commentator chatter)

00:08:44.793 --> 00:08:46.911
Not only am I comfortable
being an outsider,

00:08:46.911 --> 00:08:49.571
that has become a source
of motivation for me.

00:08:49.571 --> 00:08:52.190
So when I go to these places and you boo,

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:56.890
it actually comforts me. (laughs)

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.317
- [Commentator] They'd love
to get it to Nash's hands,

00:08:58.317 --> 00:09:00.074
and they do!
- [Commentator] They do.

00:09:00.074 --> 00:09:02.321
- [Commentator] Ball knocked
away, stolen by Parker.

00:09:02.321 --> 00:09:04.324
Here comes George, to Kobe Bryant.

00:09:04.324 --> 00:09:08.157
Bryant inside, it's good!
It's good! Tie game!

00:09:09.388 --> 00:09:12.097
- [Commentator] A one point game.

00:09:12.097 --> 00:09:14.743
Walton to tip it, Bryant with the save.

00:09:14.743 --> 00:09:15.789
- [Commentator] Now you
got to get a shot here.

00:09:15.789 --> 00:09:20.127
- [Commentator] Final seconds.
Bryant for the win. Bang!

00:09:20.127 --> 00:09:23.544
Kobe Bryant has hit a shot at the buzzer!

00:09:25.205 --> 00:09:27.583
- [Man] That he gets to the
gym at 4:30 in the morning

00:09:27.583 --> 00:09:29.934
to see Kobe just drenched in sweat,

00:09:29.934 --> 00:09:33.208
like he jumped in a pool, and
then Kobe wants to make him

00:09:33.208 --> 00:09:35.662
do conditioning and
weights for a couple hours.

00:09:35.662 --> 00:09:37.937
So then when the trainer
goes to sleep after,

00:09:37.937 --> 00:09:40.582
for a few hours, he comes back
in the gym at like 11 a.m.

00:09:40.582 --> 00:09:44.170
And he sees that Kobe never
left the gym at all because

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:47.095
he had to make sure that he
made 800 shots before he left,

00:09:47.095 --> 00:09:50.097
after he's been working
out for hours and hours.

00:09:50.097 --> 00:09:51.536
Like "You think this is new to me?"

00:09:51.536 --> 00:09:54.757
This is an excerpt from Shaq's
book, talking about Kobe.

00:09:54.757 --> 00:09:56.116
Look, they had a feud, so he says,

00:09:56.116 --> 00:09:58.886
"He was so young and so
immature in some ways,

00:09:58.886 --> 00:10:03.364
but I can tell you this,
everything Kobe is doing now,

00:10:03.364 --> 00:10:06.937
he told me all the way back
then he was going to do it.

00:10:06.937 --> 00:10:09.322
We were sitting on the
bus once, and he told me

00:10:09.322 --> 00:10:12.220
I'm going to be the #1
scorer for the Lakers,

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:14.671
I'm going to win five
or six championships,

00:10:14.671 --> 00:10:17.496
and I'm going to be the
best player in the game.

00:10:17.496 --> 00:10:19.400
And I was like 'Okay, whatever.'

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:22.817
Then he looked me right
in the eye and said,

00:10:22.817 --> 00:10:25.955
'I'm going to be the
Will Smith of the NBA.'"

00:10:25.955 --> 00:10:30.388
Shaq used to say, he would
catch Kobe Bryant on the gym,

00:10:30.388 --> 00:10:33.847
in the court, without a
ball practicing plays.

00:10:33.847 --> 00:10:36.379
This is who he is. It's
just ingrained in him

00:10:36.379 --> 00:10:38.929
to do what ever he can for a slight edge.

00:10:38.929 --> 00:10:41.100
And Shaq said, "This
is funny looking, but,

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:43.355
ya know, it probably helped him."

00:10:43.355 --> 00:10:46.345
See a lot of people say that
they're going to do something.

00:10:46.345 --> 00:10:49.416
Kobe Bryant does it. Talk
is cheap, but Kobe did it,

00:10:49.416 --> 00:10:52.522
because he competes with
himself every single day.

00:10:52.522 --> 00:10:55.309
He wants more out of
himself every single day.

00:10:55.309 --> 00:10:59.788
It's that competitive drive to
be the best that carries him.

00:10:59.788 --> 00:11:02.389
Carries him through practices.
It carries him through

00:11:02.389 --> 00:11:04.438
the weight training
sessions, conditioning.

00:11:04.438 --> 00:11:08.224
Making sure he gets 800 shots every day.

00:11:08.224 --> 00:11:11.833
It carries him to work on his
craft when no one is watching.

00:11:11.833 --> 00:11:13.834
(hip hop beat)

00:11:13.834 --> 00:11:16.196
- [Commentator] Four away from
Elgin Baylor's Laker record.

00:11:16.196 --> 00:11:18.860
(cheers) Yes!

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.496
- [Commentator] Well, there's 70.

00:11:20.496 --> 00:11:22.675
- [Commentator] Everybody wants
it to get into Kobe's hands.

00:11:22.675 --> 00:11:27.510
